Hide pathhide-matched files from /proc/<pid>/maps, smaps, smaps_rollup,
numa_maps and /proc/<pid>/fd (readdir, lookup, readlink and fdinfo).

Generated hunk by hunk against the real tree the fleet pins for this kernel
version:

    OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_common_oneplus_sm8650 @ oneplus/sm8650_b_16.0.0_pad2

and dry-run at fuzz 0 against every distinct fs/proc variant the manifests
resolve to. A hunk that only lands "with fuzz" can silently guard the wrong
function, so treat a fuzz report from `patch` as a failure and regenerate.

Version notes:
  * proc_readfd_count()/proc_fd_getattr() do not exist here -- N/A, not skipped.
  * The fleet's 6.1 trees carry TWO shapes of show_map()/show_smap(): some open
    with `struct vm_area_struct *vma = v;`, others with get_pad_vma()/
    get_data_vma(). Wrapping the function is the only form that is correct for
    both -- it needs no knowledge of the declarations, and it decides before the
    pad copies (freed only by show_map_pad_vma()) are ever allocated, so it
    cannot leak them. That is also why the wrapper hunk carries a single line of
    trailing context: the declarations below the brace are the part that differs.
  * smaps_rollup is a do/while here, so `continue` reaches the advance.
